  "info": {
    "title": "Bus Room",
    "author": "Atomik",
    "notes": "A steady four-on-the-floor tune in A minor at 118 BPM, built to be mixed: synthesised drums, a gritty bass, a soft electric keys arpeggio, a slow pad and a reedy lead. The beat ducks for a breakdown, the pad swells in and the lead opens its filter, all by automation. The mixing side: drum pads on their own channels into a Drums bus, a track folder that plays into a Music bus, group levels, two send effects, a mix-bus finish and automation of a filter, a fader and a group level."
  },
